{
  "configuration_id": "config_024",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_031 (multimodal, scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, concat) achieved 0.532 accuracy, a massive jump over both image-only baselines (~0.21–0.23). However, we have no RNA-only result, so it is unclear whether the RNA encoder alone accounts for most of this gain or whether the image modality contributes meaningfully. Question: config_024 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) is a direct ablation of the image modality from config_031, holding the RNA encoder and profile setting identical. It isolates the marginal contribution of the image branch. Why best next: Resolving whether images add real value is the single most consequential design question for the remaining budget. If RNA alone matches ~0.53, subsequent effort should focus on RNA encoder/aggregation choices; if it falls well below, images are essential and we should prioritize fusion strategy and image encoder comparisons. No other single experiment reduces this core uncertainty as cleanly."
}

